          "type": "statement",
          "say": "Together they give inverse Ackermann time per operation. That function is at most four for any input you could ever store, so in practice it is constant.",
          "props": {
            "text": "O(α(n)) — <em>effectively constant</em>.",
            "sub": "α is the inverse Ackermann function: α(n) ≤ 4 for any n that fits in memory. Either optimization alone gives O(log n).",
